# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# The rules below are written to be NON-OVERLAPPING on Cache-Control. An earlier
# version set an immutable cache on /css/* and /js/* and a revalidating one on
# /*, which both match /css/base.css — and relying on a host's precedence rules
# to resolve that is exactly the assumption this file should not make. Security
# headers live in /* and set no Cache-Control; caching is decided per path.
#
# The immutable rules are only safe because every local css/js reference carries
# ?v=<content hash>, so a changed file is a changed URL. `scaffold.py check`
# fails the build if any reference is unversioned — including on generated
# pages, which is how that invariant was broken once already.

# Versioned assets. The query is part of the browser's cache key, so a content
# change produces a new URL and the old entry is simply never asked for again.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# NOT immutable, and this is the exception that proves the rule above. Nothing
# under /assets/ is content-addressed: og.png is referenced as a bare
# https://sipi.work/assets/og.png in every page's og:image and twitter:image,
# favicon.svg and apple-touch-icon.png are bare <link> hrefs, and the logos are
# bare url() calls inside components.css. A year of immutable caching on a fixed
# URL means a replaced image never reaches anyone who already has it, including
# every social platform that has already scraped the card. That is not
# hypothetical: the launch card said "SI & PI" and "siandpi.com", and replacing
# the file could not have reached a cache that already held the old one.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

# Everything else — HTML, JSON, the licences, the changelog — is unversioned and
# must revalidate, or a deploy never reaches anyone who has visited before.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.md
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Security headers for every path. No Cache-Control here, deliberately.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
